# Claude Opus 4.4 - findings by Big Pickle (excluded)

- Source: OpenCode (`opencode/big-pickle`)
- Date: 2026-10-22 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Status: **excluded - no such model exists in Anthropic's published line-up**, so no scores are
  reported in this file.

## Model card

- **Claimed name:** Claude Opus 4.4 (folder slug `claude-opus-4.4`, id `opencode/claude-opus-4.4`).
- **Finding:** Anthropic has never released a Claude Opus 4.4. The Opus 4.x line goes
  **4 -> 4.1 -> 4.5 -> 4.6 -> 4.7 -> 4.8 -> 5 -> 5.5**; there is no 4.2, 4.3 or 4.4 in any
  first-party source, and the folder's placeholder meta ("128K total", "Text in/out",
  "Standard pricing") matches the generic scaffold, not any real spec.
- **Context window / modalities / pricing:** unknown - the model does not exist.
- **Access:** not served on OpenCode Zen (the live catalogue lists `claude-opus-4-5`,
  `claude-opus-4-6`, `claude-opus-4-7`, `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-opus-5`, `claude-opus-5-5`,
  `claude-opus-5-5-backup` - no 4.4). `opencode/claude-opus-4.4` therefore resolves to no route.

### Raw benchmarks found

- No verified public benchmark score found for Claude Opus 4.4 in any first-party or independent
  source: no Anthropic model page, no system card, no API id, no pricing row, no Artificial
  Analysis / Epoch AI / Vals AI / SWE-bench row.
- Every "4.4" sighting on the open web is derivative and self-contradictory:
  - a Copilot-compatibility shim in a third-party GitHub repo maps `claude-opus-4-6` to a
    `claude-opus-4.4` string (an internal alias, not a release);
  - a JPMorgan webcast slide transcript (2026-06-24) mentions "Claude Opus 4.4" in an AA
    Intelligence Index chart, while an AA chart transcription lists "Claude Opus 4.4" at the
    lowest output-token value - mutually inconsistent and unverifiable;
  - a machine-translated energy blog (2026-03) invents a whole "Opus 4.3 / 4.4 / Sonnet 4.3 / 4.4"
    ladder that no vendor ever shipped;
  - a 2025 LinkedIn post uses "Claude Opus 4.4" as a typo for Claude Opus 4.
- No long-context, coding, tool-use, reasoning or multimodal number exists to normalize.

## Signature

- Provided by: **Big Pickle (opencode/big-pickle)** - 2026-10-22
- Method: checked first-party sources first - the Claude models overview (current and legacy
  lineup), the model deprecations table (full lifecycle history back to 2024), and the full
  pricing table (Opus 4, 4.1, 4.5, 4.6, 4.7, 4.8, 5, 5.5 only) - then the live OpenRouter model
  list (`anthropic/claude-opus-*` = 4.1, 4.5, 4.6, 4.7, 4.8, 5, 5.5) and the live OpenCode Zen
  catalogue (no 4.4 id). Searches for the exact string "Claude Opus 4.4" returned only derivative
  artifacts (a name-translation shim, a slide transcript, a machine-translated energy table, a
  typo), none of which is a vendor announcement, model card or benchmark result. Scores are
  withheld rather than fabricated; the nearest real neighbours are Claude Opus 4.1 (retired
  2026-08-05) and Claude Opus 4.5 (2025-11-24, $5/$25, 200K context), and this report should not
  be read as a proxy for either.
- Future sources: if a genuine Claude Opus 4.4 appears, add `Claude_Opus_4_4.md` with the standard
  headings; do not edit this exclusion.
